# Operational state at the repo root only. This rule used to be an unanchored
# `state/`, which cost two files: it swallowed
# apps/web/src/app/api/entities/[slug]/state/route.ts — a live API route the
# treasury MCP calls to check whether an entity is paused — and, because git
# never descends into an excluded *directory*, it also silenced the working
# `state/* + !state/config.example.json` pair in infra/chain/.gitignore. Both
# files existed on every developer's disk and in no clone. scripts/checks/
# no-ignored-source.sh now fails the build on the next one.
/state/
*.log
.DS_Store
/data-local/
